-- title:
--   Freeness of the guarded Σ-corner over its corner ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero with finite residue field, a prime $p \neq 2$ lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and a residual representation $\bar\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a two-dimensional space over the residue field, factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ and absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure of the residue field). Assume: a finite set $S$ of primes with $p \in S$; a nonzero level $M$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2 \nmid M$; a subset $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ containing $p$ which, away from $p$, consists exactly of the primes where $\bar\rho$ is ramified, these dividing $M$, while primes $q \neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $M$ divide it at least twice and never three times, with inertia at each $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, unipotent and $\bar\rho$ ordinary at $p$ when $p \mid M$; an auxiliary prime $r \notin S$ with $r \nmid M$, $p \nmid r-1$ and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $r$ attached to a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $r$; weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ have an integral structure; and a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the anemic Hecke algebra at level $M$, weight $2$, outside $S$ to the residue field with $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ of characteristic polynomial $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$ for all $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$. Let $L = Mr$, let $H \leq (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction modulo $r$, and let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, acting $\mathcal O$-compatibly on $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal O)$, equipped with a corner datum $cd$ (an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T$, an index, and a level pairing on the resulting corner ring and corner submodule) whose corner module is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. Let $t_{\mathrm{full}}$ and $c_{\mathrm{full}}$ assign to each generator in $\mathrm{Gen}(L,S)$ (the $T_\ell$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$; the $U_q$ for $q \mid L$; the diamonds $\langle d \rangle$) an element of $\mathbb T$ and of $\mathcal O$. The hypotheses on these data, summarised here, are: every element of $\mathbb T$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the guarded operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ (those generators whose $U_q$ occurrences satisfy $q \mid M$); $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as $\mathrm{opFamily}(g)$ for guarded $g$; $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g) - c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ lies in the splitting's maximal ideal at the chosen index; cofullness, namely any $v \in H^1$ on which each $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g) - c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ is topologically nilpotent modulo every power of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ lies in the corner submodule; residual pins $c_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell) \equiv \theta(T_\ell)$, $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q) \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ for $q \neq p$ with $q^2 \mid M$, $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)$ a unit when $p \mid M$, and $c_{\mathrm{full}}(\langle d\rangle) \equiv 1$; the corner submodule is nonzero; the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module; and an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e$ of the corner ring with the localised Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^S(M)_\theta$ carrying each $T_\ell$ to the operator $\mathrm{heckeT}$ on $H^1$. Under these hypotheses the corner module is free as a module over the corner ring.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one assertion in the Taylor–Wiles argument: the $\theta$-corner of the cohomology at level $L = Mr$ is free over its corner ring, identified with the local anemic Hecke algebra at level $M$. It is stated in the corner-datum currency used by the full-corner chain, and feeds [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_sigmaPin_pairing_eq_bfam_and_free`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_sigmaPin_pairing_eq_bfam_and_free).
